      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Key rules",
          "list": [
            "Can / Can't: permission and ability.",
            "Must / Mustn't: strong obligation and prohibition.",
            "Have to / Don't have to: external obligation and no obligation.",
            "Imperative: base form of the verb. Negative: Don't + verb.",
            "Modal verbs do not change form (no -s with he/she/it)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Common mistakes",
          "list": [
            "Do not use 'to' after a modal: 'You must to go' is wrong.",
            "Do not add -s to modals: 'She musts' is wrong.",
            "Do not confuse 'mustn't' (forbidden) with 'don't have to' (not necessary)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Useful phrases",
